# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated artefact: data/modules/index.js
#
# This file is the merged output of `data/modules/postbuild.js` (TypeScript
# build + legacy_runtime.js + every other top-level *.js module). It is
# 77 000+ lines long and merging two parents line-by-line is what produced
# the cbeacf6 outage (Nakama refused to start the JS runtime because the
# merge committed `<<<<<<< HEAD` markers into the bundle).
#
# Two safety nets are wired here:
#
#   1. `merge=regen-modules-index`
#      Custom merge driver — defined in scripts/git-merge-regen-index.sh —
#      ignores both sides and re-runs `node postbuild.js` so the output
#      always matches the source files. Activate it once per clone with:
#        scripts/setup-hooks.sh
#      (or manually: `git config merge.regen-modules-index.driver
#       'scripts/git-merge-regen-index.sh %A'`).
#
#   2. `linguist-generated=true`
#      Hides the file from PR diff views on GitHub so reviewers stop
#      manually 'fixing' a generated file.
#
# Same treatment for the TS compile output committed for offline builds.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/modules/index.js          merge=regen-modules-index linguist-generated=true
data/modules/build/index.js    merge=regen-modules-index linguist-generated=true
data/modules/build/index.d.ts  linguist-generated=true

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Line endings for anything a POSIX shell or the Docker builder parses.
#
# Commit 4239b28ef added scripts/ecr-digest.sh and
# scripts/assert-deploy-account.sh from a Windows workstation with CRLF
# endings, and deploy-eks.yml sources them in its *first* step. Sourcing a
# CRLF file under bash appends \r to every token, so the step died with
#   scripts/ecr-digest.sh: line 10: $'\r': command not found   (exit 127)
# and every push to master built and deployed nothing for 15 days
# (2026-08-25 → 2026-08-29; last green run 2026-08-10).
#
# `text eol=lf` forces LF into the index *and* the working tree regardless
# of the committer's core.autocrlf, so the same mistake cannot be
# reintroduced from a Windows checkout. `.github/workflows/preflight`-style
# enforcement also lives in deploy-eks.yml ("Reject CRLF in shell scripts")
# because .gitattributes only protects paths that go through git's
# normalisation, and a guard that runs in CI is the one that actually gates
# the deploy.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf

# PowerShell helpers are Windows-native and intentionally CRLF. Pinned
# explicitly so they are never caught by a future blanket `* text=auto`
# and so their endings are a stated decision rather than an accident.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf
